f nursing science Demonstrate advanced clinical nursing competencies Function as Cli\nnical Nurse Specialists and nurse managers Promote interprofessional collaboration in healthcare teams Plan, lead, and evaluate healthcare programmes Conduct and utilise nursing re\nsearch Function as nurse educators and mentors Encourage continuous professional development Specialties Offered Medical-Surgical Nursing Cardiovascular & Thoracic Nursing Critical\n Care Nursing Oncology Nursing Neurosciences Nursing Nephro-Urology Nursing Orthopedic Nursing Gastroenterology Nursing Obstetric & Gynecological Nursing Child Health (Paediatric) \n--\nsity examinations are conducted in September/October , with supplementary examinations held in November/December , as per MPMSU guidelines. Students must maintain 80% attendance in\n theory and 100% attendance in practicals . Internal assessments are conducted as per university norms. Award of Degree Successful candidates are awarded the Master of Science (Nur\nsing) degree and are eligible for registration with the Nursing Council of any State in India. Take the First Step Towards a Professional Nursing Career Begin your journey towards \na rewarding and respected career in healthcare with Career College of Nursing, Bhopal , where academic excellence meets compassionate patient care. Apply Now --> Contact Admissions\n Career College of Nursing Opposite BHEL Dussehra Maidan, Sector A, Govindpura, Bhopal, Madhya Pradesh 462023 Email: info@careercollegeindia.com Office Phone: 8959007700 Group Inst\nitution • CCB • CIMS • CCL • CCM --> • CDS Quick Links • Nursing blog • Nursing Facebook • Nursing Youtube • Nursing linkedin • MIS Login • Grievance Important links • INC • MPMSU \n• MPNRC • NAAC • Anti-Ragging Helpline • Student Feedback • Parents Feedback • Alumni Feedback • Employer Feedback Connect With Us © 2026 Career College of Nursing, Bhopal. Affilia\nted to Barkatullah University,Bhopal Approved by the Indian Nursing Council (INC), New Delhi, and the M.P. Nurses Registration Council (MPNRC), Bhopal. All Rights Reserved. &times;\n Enquire Now Book your appointment today! Name Phone Number Date of Appointment Type of Cancer Select type of cancer Breast Cancer Lung Cancer Prostate Cancer Colorectal Cancer Ski\nn Cancer Leukemia Lymphoma Pancreatic Cancer Ovarian Cancer Oral Cancer Bladder Cancer Kidney Cancer Esophageal Cancer Brain Cancer Other State / City Submit Request a Callback Nam\n=== bsc-nursing ===\n Career College of Nursing Bhopal A Premier Nursing Institution Shaping Future Healthcare Professionals Home About Us About College Aim, Vision and Mission Chairman's Message From \nThe Principal's Desk --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> -->\n --> --> Infrastructure Classrooms Nursing Foundation including Adult Health Nursing Lab Paediatric Lab Pre-Clinical Sciences Lab Obstetrics and Gynaecology Lab Nutrition Lab Advan\nce Science Lab Library Computer Lab. Courses M.Sc. Nursing B.Sc. Nursing G.N.M. (General Nursing and Midwifery) Academics Academic Calendar Syllabus Prospectus --> --> --> --> Gall\nery Functional Units Student Nurses Association (SNA) Activity Internal Quality Assurance Cell (IQAC) Training and Placement Cell Student Satisfaction Research Unit (SSRU) Green Cl\nuster Women Empowerment Anti-Ragging Committee Grievance and Redressal Cell Personality Assessment and Development Cell Alumni Cell Library Cell National Cadet Corps (NCC) National\n--\n-> Infrastructure --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> In\nfrastructure Classrooms Nursing Foundation including Adult Health Nursing Lab Paediatric Lab Pre-Clinical Sciences Lab Obstetrics and Gynaecology Lab Nutrition Lab Advance Science \nLab Library Computer Lab. Courses M.Sc. Nursing B.Sc. Nursing G.N.M. (General Nursing and Midwifery) Academics Academic Calendar Syllabus Prospectus Faculty Functional Units Studen\nt Nurses Association (SNA) Activity Internal Quality Assurance Cell (IQAC) Training and Placement Cell Student Satisfaction Research Unit (SSRU) Blogs Contact Student Notice Board \n--> B.Sc. Nursing Building Competent Nursing Professionals Undergraduate programme preparing students to deliver safe, effective, and compassionate nursing care across hospitals an\nd community settings. Duration 4 Years Medium English Degree Awarded By Barkatullah Vishwavidyalaya Programme Overview The Bachelor of Science in Nursing (B.Sc. Nursing) program pr\nepares students to deliver safe, effective, and compassionate nursing care in hospitals and community settings. It integrates foundational sciences, nursing theory, and clinical ex\nperience to build competence and confidence. Eligibility Criteria 10+2 (Science stream) with 45% marks (PCB) from a recognized board Candidates from State Open School or NIOS with \nScience and English are eligible Candidate must have completed 17 years of age on or before 31st December of the admission year 5% relaxation in marks for SC/ST candidates Reservat\nions as per State Government Policy Programme Objectives Apply knowledge from physical, biological, and behavioural sciences in holistic care Demonstrate nursing skills and techniq\nues using evidence-based practice Deliver comprehensive care to individuals, families, and communities Apply critical thinking and decision-making in complex healthcare situations \nTake up leadership roles as first-line managers in healthcare and education Participate in promotive, preventive, and restorative healthcare Conduct nursing research and apply find\nings in practice Exhibit moral and ethical values in professional conduct Course Structure Year Core Subjects First Year Anatomy, Physiology, Nutrition, Biochemistry, Nursing Found\nations, Psychology, Microbiology, English, Computer Introduction Second Year Sociology, Medical–Surgical Nursing–I, Pharmacology, Pathology, Genetics, Community Health Nursing–I, C\nommunication & Educational Technology Third Year Medical–Surgical Nursing–II, Child Health Nursing, Mental Health Nursing, Nursing Research & Statistics Final Year Midwifery & Obst\netrical Nursing, Community Health Nursing–II, Management of Nursing Services & Education Examination System Examinations are conducted in September/October , with supplementary exa\nms in November/December as per MPMSU schedule. Students must maintain 80% attendance in theory and 100% in practicals . Internal assessments follow university norms. Award of Degre\ne Successful candidates are awarded the Bachelor of Science (Nursing) degree and are eligible for registration with any State Nursing Council in India. Take the First Step Towards \na Professional Nursing Career Begin your journey towards a rewarding and respected career in healthcare with Career College of Nursing, Bhopal , where academic excellence meets com\npassionate patient care. Apply Now --> Contact Admissions Career College of Nursing Opposite BHEL Dussehra Maidan, Sector A, Govindpura, Bhopal, Madhya Pradesh 462023 Email: info@c\nareercollegeindia.com Office Phone: 8959007700 Group Institution • CCB • CIMS • CCL • CCM --> • CDS Quick Links • Nursing blog • Nursing Facebook • Nursing Youtube • Nursing linked\nin • MIS Login • Grievance Important links • INC • MPMSU • MPNRC • NAAC • Anti-Ragging Helpline • Student Feedback • Parents Feedback • Alumni Feedback • Employer Feedback Connect \nWith Us © 2026 Career College of Nursing, Bhopal. Affiliated to Barkatullah University,Bhopal Approved by the Indian Nursing Council (INC), New Delhi, and the M.P. Nurses Registrat\nion Council (MPNRC), Bhopal. All Rights Reserved. &times; Enquire Now Book your appointment today! Name Phone Number Date of Appointment Type of Cancer Select type of cancer Breast\n Cancer Lung Cancer Prostate Cancer Colorectal Cancer Skin Cancer Leukemia Lymphoma Pancreatic Cancer Ovarian Cancer Oral Cancer Bladder Cancer Kidney Cancer Esophageal Cancer Brai\nn Cancer Other State / City Submit Request a Callback Name Phone Number Query Submit \n=== gnm-nursing ===\n Career College of Nursing Bhopal A Premier Nursing Institution Shaping Future Healthcare Professionals Home About Us About College Aim, Vision and Mission Chairman's Message From \nThe Principal's Desk --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> -->\n --> --> Infrastructure Classrooms Nursing Foundation including Adult Health Nursing Lab Paediatric Lab Pre-Clinical Sciences Lab Obstetrics and Gynaecology Lab Nutrition Lab Advan\nce Science Lab Library Computer Lab. Courses M.Sc. Nursing B.Sc. Nursing G.N.M. (General Nursing and Midwifery) Academics Academic Calendar Syllabus Prospectus --> --> --> --> Gall\nery Functional Units Student Nurses Association (SNA) Activity Internal Quality Assurance Cell (IQAC) Training and Placement Cell Student Satisfaction Research Unit (SSRU) Green Cl\nuster Women Empowerment Anti-Ragging Committee Grievance and Redressal Cell Personality Assessment and Development Cell Alumni Cell Library Cell National Cadet Corps (NCC) National\n--\n-> Infrastructure --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> --> In\nfrastructure Classrooms Nursing Foundation including Adult Health Nursing Lab Paediatric Lab Pre-Clinical Sciences Lab Obstetrics and Gynaecology Lab Nutrition Lab Advance Science \nLab Library Computer Lab. Courses M.Sc. Nursing B.Sc. Nursing G.N.M. (General Nursing and Midwifery) Academics Academic Calendar Syllabus Prospectus Faculty Functional Units Studen\nt Nurses Association (SNA) Activity Internal Quality Assurance Cell (IQAC) Training and Placement Cell Student Satisfaction Research Unit (SSRU) Blogs Contact Student Notice Board \n--> G.N.M. (General Nursing and Midwifery) Preparing Competent & Caring Nurses The G.N.M. programme prepares students to become competent and caring nurses who can function effecti\nvely in hospitals and community settings. Duration 3 Years Medium English Examination Board Madhya Pradesh Nurses Registration Council, Bhopal Programme Overview The G.N.M. program\nme focuses on developing the knowledge, skills, and attitudes essential for nursing practice. Students learn to provide safe, effective, and compassionate care in hospitals and com\nmunity settings. Eligibility Criteria 10+2 with English and a minimum of 40% marks in aggregate from a recognised board Candidates from State Open School or NIOS with English are e\nligible 10+2 with ANM (Vocational) or Health Care Science (Vocational) with 40% marks are also eligible Registered ANMs with pass marks are accepted Age limit: 17–35 years (as on 3\n1st December of admission year) 5% relaxation for SC/ST candidates Reservations as per State Government Policy Programme Objectives Demonstrate competency in providing holistic hea\nlthcare to individuals and families Apply knowledge from biological and behavioural sciences in nursing practice Collaborate effectively with healthcare teams Provide curative, pre\nventive, and rehabilitative services Demonstrate ethical values and professional responsibility Participate in professional organizations and continuing education Demonstrate teach\ning and administrative skills in healthcare settings Assist in community-based research activities Course Structure Year Core Subjects First Year Anatomy & Physiology, Microbiology\n, Psychology, Sociology, Fundamentals of Nursing, First Aid, Community Health Nursing–I, Environmental Hygiene, Nutrition, English, Computer Education Second Year Medical–Surgical \nNursing–I & II, Mental Health Nursing, Child Health Nursing Third Year Part I Midwifery & Gynecological Nursing, Community Health Nursing–II Third Year Part II Nursing Education, I\nntroduction to Research, Professional Trends & Adjustments, Nursing Administration & Ward Management Examination System Annual examinations are conducted by the MP Nurses Registrat\nion Council in August/September , with supplementary exams held every six months. Students must complete 11 months of coursework with 80% attendance in theory and 100% in practical\ns . Absences must be compensated during summer vacations. Award of Diploma Successful candidates are awarded a Diploma in General Nursing and Midwifery (G.N.M.) by the Madhya Prade\nsh Nurses Registration Council, Bhopal, and are eligible for registration with the Nursing Council of any State in India. Take the First Step Towards a Professional Nursing Career \nBegin your journey towards a rewarding and respected career in healthcare with Career College of Nursing, Bhopal , where academic excellence meets compassionate patient care. Apply\n Now --> Contact Admissions Career College of Nursing Opposite BHEL Dussehra Maidan, Sector A, Govindpura, Bhopal, Madhya Pradesh 462023 Email: info@careercollegeindia.com Office P\nhone: 8959007700 Group Institution • CCB • CIMS • CCL • CCM --> • CDS Quick Links • Nursing blog • Nursing Facebook • Nursing Youtube • Nursing linkedin • MIS Login • Grievance Imp\nortant links • INC • MPMSU • MPNRC • NAAC • Anti-Ragging Helpline • Student Feedback • Parents Feedback • Alumni Feedback • Employer Feedback Connect With Us © 2026 Career College \nof Nursing, Bhopal. Affiliated to Barkatullah University,Bhopal Approved by the Indian Nursing Council (INC), New Delhi, and the M.P. Nurses Registration Council (MPNRC), Bhopal. A\nll Rights Reserved. &times; Enquire Now Book your appointment today! Name Phone Number Date of Appointment Type of Cancer Select type of cancer Breast Cancer Lung Cancer Prostate C\nancer Colorectal Cancer Skin Cancer Leukemia Lymphoma Pancreatic Cancer Ovarian Cancer Oral Cancer Bladder Cancer Kidney Ca