{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'work=$(find \"$TMPDIR\" -maxdepth 1 -type d -name '\"'career-college-nursing.*' | tail -n 1)\nfor f in msc bsc gnm; do\n echo \\\"--- \"'$f eligibility html ---\"\n rg -in -C 5 '\"'eligib' \\\"\"'$work/$f.html\" | sed -n '\"'1,180p'\ndone\"","aggregated_output":"--- msc eligibility html ---\n568-                expertise, and academic excellence.\r\n569-            </p>\r\n570-        </div>\r\n571-\r\n572-        <div class=\"msc-card\">\r\n573:            <h3>Eligibility <span class=\"text-thm\">Criteria</span></h3>\r\n574-            <ul class=\"msc-list\">\r\n575-                <li>Registered Nurse and Registered Midwife with any State Nursing Council</li>\r\n576-                <li>B.Sc. Nursing / B.Sc. (Hons.) Nursing / Post Basic B.Sc. Nursing with minimum 55% marks</li>\r\n577-                <li>Completion of B.Sc. Nursing or equivalent with proper clinical exposure</li>\r\n578-                <li>Minimum one year of work experience after Basic or Post Basic B.Sc. Nursing</li>\r\n--\n631-\r\n632-        <div class=\"msc-card highlight-card\">\r\n633-            <h3>Award of <span class=\"text-thm\">Degree</span></h3>\r\n634-            <p>\r\n635-                Successful candidates are awarded the <strong>Master of Science (Nursing)</strong>\r\n636:                degree and are eligible for registration with the Nursing Council of any State in India.\r\n637-            </p>\r\n638-\r\n639-        </div>\r\n640-\r\n641-    </div>\r\n--- bsc eligibility html ---\n680-                The Bachelor of Science in Nursing (B.Sc. Nursing) program prepares students to deliver safe, effective, and compassionate nursing care in hospitals and community settings. It integrates foundational sciences, nursing theory, and clinical experience to build competence and confidence.\r\n681-            </p>\r\n682-        </div>\r\n683-\r\n684-        <div class=\"bsc-card\">\r\n685:            <h3>Eligibility <span class=\"text-thm\">Criteria</span></h3>\r\n686-            <ul class=\"bsc-list\">\r\n687-                <li>10+2 (Science stream) with 45% marks (PCB) from a recognized board</li>\r\n688:                <li>Candidates from State Open School or NIOS with Science and English are eligible</li>\r\n689-                <li>Candidate must have completed 17 years of age on or before 31st December of the admission year</li>\r\n690-                <li>5% relaxation in marks for SC/ST candidates</li>\r\n691-                <li>Reservations as per State Government Policy</li>\r\n692-            </ul>\r\n693-        </div>\r\n--\n752-        </div>\r\n753-\r\n754-        <div class=\"bsc-card highlight-card\">\r\n755-            <h3>Award of <span class=\"text-thm\">Degree</span></h3>\r\n756-            <p>\r\n757:                Successful candidates are awarded the <strong>Bachelor of Science (Nursing)</strong> degree and are eligible for registration with any State Nursing Council in India.\r\n758-            </p>\r\n759-\r\n760-        </div>\r\n761-        </div>\r\n762-\r\n--- gnm eligibility html ---\n680-                The G.N.M. programme focuses on developing the knowledge, skills, and attitudes essential for nursing practice. Students learn to provide safe, effective, and compassionate care in hospitals and community settings.\r\n681-            </p>\r\n682-        </div>\r\n683-\r\n684-        <div class=\"bsc-card\">\r\n685:            <h3>Eligibility <span class=\"text-thm\">Criteria</span></h3>\r\n686-            <ul class=\"bsc-list\">\r\n687-                <li>10+2 with English and a minimum of 40% marks in aggregate from a recognised board</li>\r\n688:                <li>Candidates from State Open School or NIOS with English are eligible</li>\r\n689:                <li>10+2 with ANM (Vocational) or Health Care Science (Vocational) with 40% marks are also eligible</li>\r\n690-                <li>Registered ANMs with pass marks are accepted</li>\r\n691-                <li>Age limit: 17–35 years (as on 31st December of admission year)</li>\r\n692-                <li>5% relaxation for SC/ST candidates</li>\r\n693-                <li>Reservations as per State Government Policy</li>\r\n694-            </ul>\r\n--\n752-        </div>\r\n753-\r\n754-        <div class=\"bsc-card highlight-card\">\r\n755-            <h3>Award of <span class=\"text-thm\">Diploma</span></h3>\r\n756-            <p>\r\n757:                Successful candidates are awarded a <strong>Diploma in General Nursing and Midwifery (G.N.M.)</strong> by the Madhya Pradesh Nurses Registration Council, Bhopal, and are eligible for registration with the Nursing Council of any State in India.\r\n758-            </p>\r\n759-\r\n760-        </div>\r\n761-\r\n762-    </div>\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
